{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503615-stuff-stuck-in-elsewhere","id":1503615,"title":"Stuff stuck in Elsewhere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-21T05:43:49-08:00","id":1503615,"title":"Stuff stuck in Elsewhere","content":"I had a thought about Elsewhere the other day. One must imagine that plenty of exalts have died while their artefacts were still hidden away in Elsewhere. Stuff in Elsewhere is perfectly safe and doesn't decay. Those artefacts are still there.<br /> I recall a story about some adventurous solar trying to travel to Elsewhere to retrieve these artefacts and getting stuck in a weird kind of stasis, alive and aware but unable to do anything.<br /> So question: Can things in Elsewhere be retrieved by someone that is not the person that stuck them there? How difficult should this be? Would you need a sorcerous working to manage it?<br /> Obviously in game terms, you don't want to make it too easy or the players are going to go around pulling all kinds of things out that you don't necessarily want them to have.<br /> <br /> So many the solution would be:<br /> 1) yes you can retrieve stuff stuck in Elsewhere.<br /> 2) It requires a sorcerous working.<br /> 3) you need either some link to the item to be retrieved (or to the person that put it there), or retrieval grants you access to the closest item to where the working is performed.<br /> 4) it doesn't work if the person that stashed the item is still alive in some form. The Elsewhere that they use is still under their control. This might not include ghosts (who are dead) but could include gods.<br /> <br /> This would allow for epic quests for an item/s important to some ancient solar if you want to try and retrieve his daiklave. Or you can do the working and take your changes on what you get. Maybe its a five dot grand daiklave, but maybe its just some travel rations stashed there for freshness over 2000 years ago.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T07:13:24-08:00","id":1503618,"title":"","content":"I do believe that Charms to store something Elsewhere are invariably Indefinite; they require a mote commitment to maintain their effect. I think it would make sense that mote commitments end if the Exalt behind them dies.<br /> <br /> Huh, interesting; I checked back a bit, and find that it's actually the Dragon-Blooded who can send things Elsewhere as an Instant action, with the alternative cost of needing to pass them through elemental manifestations. I think that's a case where killing the Exalt does not get immediate results, but it can be plausible that there are spirits with the power to draw things back out of such a storage method.<br /> <br /> I think the current writers would still maintain the idea that Elsewhere shouldn't be seen as some kind of common spatial pocket, it's just a descriptor for something being placed in a state of close at hand non-existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-21-2023, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T07:20:52-08:00","id":1503620,"title":"","content":"I vaguely remember the corebook mentions that objects stored in elsewhere can start to pop up all over Creation if the owner die which sounds more plausible than them being stuck \u201cthere\u201d forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T16:10:19-08:00","id":1503641,"title":"","content":"Point 4 is basically assumed. Unless the specific storage method mentions otherwise, stuff stored in Elsewhere is supposed to be perfectly safe from hijacking - at least as long as you are alive/device that sustains storage is working. Notice, that (as already mentioned), most forms of storing stuff in Elsewhere require both an anchor (a person or a storage device), and an active essence commitment. If one of those things is gone, stuff likely ends back somewhere in Creation. And (if anchor is dead/destroyed) not necessarily all in one place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T06:21:16-08:00","id":1503803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1503615-stuff-stuck-in-elsewhere?p=1503620#post1503620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely remember the corebook mentions that objects stored in elsewhere can start to pop up all over Creation if the owner die which sounds more plausible than them being stuck \u201cthere\u201d forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>and I see another story hook for why the Ursurpation happened, who is going to let human god monsters keep sniping each other while WMD artifacts fall from the sky like pennies from heaven, hell, I can see some solars doing this just for the sport of seeing how many artifacts they can get to land everywhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}